# watch.table - the jobs homehub-watch.py keeps an eye on (SN-048, SR-088).
#
# ONE ROW PER WATCH, whitespace-separated:
#   name  kind  target  threshold  [when]
#
# kind:
#   process        a process whose comm is TARGET (first 15 characters, as the
#                  kernel keeps it) has been absent for THRESHOLD.
#   unit-success   the systemd unit TARGET has not finished successfully for
#                  THRESHOLD (systemd's own record, kept across reboots in the
#                  watch's state file).
#   docker-health  any container docker reports `unhealthy` for THRESHOLD
#                  (TARGET is `*`; one alert per container).
#   docker-restarts any container whose RestartCount rose by 3 or more within
#                  THRESHOLD (TARGET is `*`; one alert per container). A crash
#                  loop never reads `unhealthy` - between deaths it is
#                  `starting` and `docker ps` says Up (open-items C58).
# threshold: Nm (minutes) or Nh (hours).
# when: comma-separated conditions on stack .env knobs, ALL of which must hold:
#   KEY=VALUE, KEY!=VALUE, or KEY (set and not empty). Omitted or `-` = always.
# ${KEY:-default} in target or threshold is replaced from the stack .env.
#
# A row is switched off without editing this file by naming it in
# HOMEHUB_WATCH_DISABLE (space-separated). Rows here are data, not code: adding
# a watch is a line in this file.
#
# name             kind           target                                      threshold                                   when
icedrive-client    process        Icedrive.AppImage                           15m                                         ICEDRIVE_MODE=appimage,REMOTE_UI_ENABLED=true
library-backup     unit-success   homehub-library-backup.service              26h                                         -
icedrive-profile   unit-success   homehub-icedrive-profile.service            26h                                         ICEDRIVE_MODE,ICEDRIVE_MODE!=off
containers         docker-health  *                                           10m                                         -
restart-loops      docker-restarts *                                          30m                                         -
# The drill target. Off unless HOMEHUB_WATCH_SYNTHETIC_PROCESS names a process;
# used only to prove the alert path end to end (stack/monitoring/README.md).
synthetic          process        ${HOMEHUB_WATCH_SYNTHETIC_PROCESS:-}        ${HOMEHUB_WATCH_SYNTHETIC_ABSENT_MIN:-10}m  HOMEHUB_WATCH_SYNTHETIC_PROCESS
